## WHO-UMC Causality Assessment

* Classification: Probable / Likely
* Rationale:
  1. Temporal Sequence: Onset occurred after 4 years of cumulative oral bisphosphonate exposure following an invasive dental trigger, matching the typical presentation profile of MRONJ.
  2. De-challenge: Healing of oral mucosa and resolution of necrotic discharge observed following drug discontinuation and conservative therapy.
  3. Exclusion of Alternatives: Prior head/neck radiation therapy, jaw metastases, and primary osteomyelitis were ruled out via clinical history and imaging.
  4. Re-challenge: Re-exposure was ethically avoided due to risks of extensive mandibular necrosis, placing causality in Probable under WHO criteria rather than Certain.

